# Frontend configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides. Neither variable below is required
# for local development -- the defaults point at a backend on port 8000.

# Where the FastAPI backend is, as seen FROM THE NEXT.JS SERVER.
#
# Used for two things: the `/api/v1/*` rewrite in next.config.ts, and the direct
# calls Server Components make. Both run on the server, which is why this is NOT
# prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` -- the API's address is never inlined into the browser
# bundle, and changing it is a restart rather than a rebuild.
#
# In production this is the internal or public URL of the backend host, e.g.
#   API_ORIGIN=https://duolingo-api.fly.dev
# API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# The name of the session cookie. MUST match SESSION_COOKIE_NAME on the backend;
# `proxy.ts` looks for a cookie with this name to decide whether a visitor is
# plausibly signed in.
# SESSION_COOKIE_NAME=duolingo_session

# --- removed in Phase 10 ---------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is gone. It was inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD
# time, so forgetting to set it in a deployment produced a site that asked every
# visitor's own machine for the API -- with no error anywhere. The browser now
# calls its own origin through the rewrite and needs no configuration at all.
